INSERT INTO [dbo].[Section] ([UpdateDate],[RevisionID],[ID],[ParentID],[DisplayOrder],[Title],[SectionContentTypeID],[TextContent],[IsInternalSection],[DisplayRateCode],[RevisionUniqueSectionId]) VALUES (GETDATE(),2,437,411,7,'541183 - Metrology',1,'',0,0,157);
INSERT INTO [dbo].[Section] ([UpdateDate],[RevisionID],[ID],[ParentID],[DisplayOrder],[Title],[SectionContentTypeID],[TextContent],[IsInternalSection],[DisplayRateCode],[RevisionUniqueSectionId]) VALUES (GETDATE(),2,438,437,0,null,2,'<p>Metrology services and related Engineering Support services performed by SSC Services Segment for the calibration of Measuring and Test Equipment (M&amp;TE). Also includes costs of outside vendor repairs/calibration and SSC labor for financial administration of the metrology process.</p> <p>Base: Metrology costs are assigned on a YTD basis to the requesting contract, LMSSC Functional Organization, LMC Business area or commercial entity based on the current month calibration hours and metrology engineering support hours reported by the LMMS Metrology Network system. Dollars are assigned based on the percentage of calibration and engineering support hours charged to each cost objective.</p>			',0,0,158);
INSERT INTO [dbo].[Section] ([UpdateDate],[RevisionID],[ID],[ParentID],[DisplayOrder],[Title],[SectionContentTypeID],[TextContent],[IsInternalSection],[DisplayRateCode],[RevisionUniqueSectionId]) VALUES (GETDATE(),2,439,411,8,'541185 - Assembly, Test and Launch Operations (ATLO) Service Center',1,'',0,0,159);
INSERT INTO [dbo].[Section] ([UpdateDate],[RevisionID],[ID],[ParentID],[DisplayOrder],[Title],[SectionContentTypeID],[TextContent],[IsInternalSection],[DisplayRateCode],[RevisionUniqueSectionId]) VALUES (GETDATE(),2,440,439,0,null,2,'<p>SSC Labor and non-labor costs incurred for multi-program management interface, resource deployment, oversight and administrative effort in support of Assembly, Test and Launch Operations personnel. Includes management and technical effort in meeting program requirements. Scope of effort includes but is not limited to: mechanical and electrical test engineering, test procedures and software, test operations, logistics, launch operations, MAGE/EAGE, EAGE software, maintenance and calibration of direct acquired equipment, material control, tool control, planning, configuration control, quality control, facility management of chambers and high-bays, material control, shipping and receiving, transportation, resource management and administration. Includes pagers, cell phones, and other comparable communications devices; travel expense incurred supporting multi-program requirements and related coordination, status and reporting efforts; depreciation, maintenance and repair for fixed asset tooling and equipment accountable to the Assembly, Test and Launch Operations Service Center.</p> <p>Base = Direct labor hours in ATLO Sending Cost Centers in the Development Overhead Pool (Core Segment)<br />Result = Labor cost in Development Pool and ODC dollars</p>			',0,0,160);
